msgstr "Latar belakang {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Julia is a dynamic programming language designed primarily for numerical and scientific computing. Its high-performance numerical computing capabilities make it a natural fit for quantum simulation workflows. In this tutorial, we show how Julia is used for both classical pre- and post-processing (for example, building Hamiltonians, running ODE (ordinary differential equation) solvers, and computing expectation values) and for orchestrating quantum hardware jobs, eliminating the need to switch between languages or environments.\n"
msgstr "Julia ialah bahasa pengaturcaraan dinamik yang direka terutamanya untuk pengkomputeran berangka dan saintifik. Keupayaan pengkomputeran berangka berprestasi tingginya menjadikannya sesuai secara semula jadi untuk aliran kerja simulasi kuantum. Dalam tutorial ini, kami menunjukkan cara Julia digunakan untuk pra- dan pasca-pemprosesan klasik (contohnya, membina Hamiltonian, menjalankan penyelesai ODE (persamaan pembezaan biasa), dan mengira nilai jangkaan) dan untuk mengorkestra job perkakasan kuantum, menghapuskan keperluan untuk bertukar antara bahasa atau persekitaran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To interface with IBM Quantum&reg; hardware from Julia, this tutorial uses two packages from the Qiskit ecosystem: `Qiskit.jl` wraps the Qiskit C library and provides circuit construction and transpilation functionality in Julia; `QiskitIBMRuntime.jl` connects to IBM Quantum hardware through the IBM Quantum Compute Service client, enabling job submission and result retrieval directly from Julia.\n"
msgstr "Untuk berhubung dengan perkakasan IBM Quantum&reg; daripada Julia, tutorial ini menggunakan dua pakej daripada ekosistem Qiskit: `Qiskit.jl` membungkus pustaka C Qiskit dan menyediakan fungsi pembinaan litar dan transpilasi dalam Julia; `QiskitIBMRuntime.jl` menyambung ke perkakasan IBM Quantum melalui klien IBM Quantum Compute Service, membolehkan penghantaran job dan pengambilan hasil terus daripada Julia.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial, we consider the trotterized evolution of the transverse-field Ising model on a 1D chain with nearest-neighbor interactions:\n"
msgstr "Dalam tutorial ini, kita mempertimbangkan evolusi ter-Trotter bagi model Ising medan melintang pada rantai 1D dengan interaksi jiran terdekat:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"    H = \\sum_{\\langle i,j\\rangle}J_{ij}Z_iZ_j + \\sum_i h_i X_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"    H = \\sum_{\\langle i,j\\rangle}J_{ij}Z_iZ_j + \\sum_i h_i X_i\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To implement the time evolution $e^{-iH\\tau}$, we divide the time interval $\\tau$ into $r$ steps and define $\\Delta\\tau=\\tau/r$. The second-order Trotter-Suzuki decomposition gives the following:\n"
"$$\n"
"    e^{-iH\\Delta\\tau}\\approx \\prod_i e^{-ih_i X_i\\Delta\\tau/2 } \\prod_{\\langle i,j\\rangle} e^{-iJ_{ij}Z_iZ_j\\Delta\\tau} \\prod_i e^{-ih_iX_i\\Delta\\tau/2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk melaksanakan evolusi masa $e^{-iH\\tau}$, kita membahagikan sela masa $\\tau$ kepada $r$ langkah dan mentakrifkan $\\Delta\\tau=\\tau/r$. Penguraian Trotter-Suzuki tertib kedua memberikan yang berikut:\n"
"$$\n"
"    e^{-iH\\Delta\\tau}\\approx \\prod_i e^{-ih_i X_i\\Delta\\tau/2 } \\prod_{\\langle i,j\\rangle} e^{-iJ_{ij}Z_iZ_j\\Delta\\tau} \\prod_i e^{-ih_iX_i\\Delta\\tau/2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For circuit construction, each Trotter step is implemented as a sequence of single-qubit $R_x$ rotations and two-qubit $R_{ZZ}$ gates. The circuit begins by preparing the Néel state $|0101\\cdots\\rangle$ using X gates on alternating qubits. Each subsequent Trotter step applies: (1) $R_x(h_i\\Delta\\tau)$ on every qubit, (2) $R_{ZZ}(2J_{ij}\\Delta\\tau)$ on each neighboring pair along the chain, and (3) $R_x(h_i\\Delta\\tau)$ again on every qubit. The total circuit depth grows linearly with the number of Trotter steps $r$.\n"
msgstr "Untuk pembinaan litar, setiap langkah Trotter dilaksanakan sebagai urutan putaran $R_x$ satu-qubit dan gate $R_{ZZ}$ dua-qubit. Litar bermula dengan menyediakan keadaan Néel $|0101\\cdots\\rangle$ menggunakan gate X pada qubit berselang-seli. Setiap langkah Trotter berikutnya mengenakan: (1) $R_x(h_i\\Delta\\tau)$ pada setiap qubit, (2) $R_{ZZ}(2J_{ij}\\Delta\\tau)$ pada setiap pasangan berjiran di sepanjang rantai, dan (3) $R_x(h_i\\Delta\\tau)$ sekali lagi pada setiap qubit. Kedalaman litar keseluruhan bertambah secara linear dengan bilangan langkah Trotter $r$.\n"

